Article 22
(1) Institutional strengthening of Women's Protection can be carried out through capacity building, cooperation and integration with:
a. government agencies;
b. educational institutions;
c. religious institutions;
d. health service provider institutions; e. professional institutions;
f. business sector;
g. service institutions;
h. Islamic boarding schools;
i. youth organizations;
j. legal aid organizations;
k. media;
l. religious leaders;
m. community leaders;
n. communities; and
o. families.
(2) Strengthening and development of Women's Protection service provider institutions is implemented through: a. capacity building of human resources of Women's Protection service provider institutions for victims of violence at the Regional level;
b. provision of specific needs for women in emergency situations and special conditions at the Regional level;
c. development of communication, information, and education strategies regarding the protection of women's rights at the Regional level;
d. strengthening networks among Women's Protection service provider institutions at the Regional level;
e. facilitation of efforts to fulfill standards of Women's Protection service provider institutions at the Regional level; f. development of Women's Protection service provider institutions at the Regional level.

